-- Work Injury Compensation Act 2019 — INDEPENDENT TESTS.
--
-- Every expected value was decided from ../source/WICA2019.txt and
-- ../source/PROVENANCE.md before any module was opened; the scenarios and
-- their provisions are listed in independent-expectations.md (the IDs in the
-- comments below, e.g. [B9], are that file's). A failing assertion here is a
-- finding, not a test to be fixed.

§ `Independent tests`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `about` x `is` y IF
    (x MINUS y) AT MOST 0.01 AND (y MINUS x) AT MOST 0.01

GIVEN c IS A `Coverage`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is covered:` c IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `not covered` r THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN l IS A `Liability`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is liable:` l IF
    CONSIDER l
    WHEN `liable to pay compensation` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN d IS A `Disease liability`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is compensable:` d IF
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `compensable as if a work injury` u THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN who IS A STRING
      shares IS A LIST OF `Operator share`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`share of` who `in` shares MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN s YIELD s's `share`) (filter (GIVEN s YIELD s's `operator` EQUALS who) shares))

GIVEN i IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`months for item` i MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Second Schedule row` i
    WHEN JUST r  THEN r's `period in months`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0

-- A claimant: capacity, Third Schedule class, and the TRUE flags by name.
GIVEN cap IS A `Capacity at work`
      cls IS A `Third Schedule class`
      flags IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A Claimant
`worker` cap cls flags MEANS
    Claimant WITH
        `name` IS "X"
        `date of birth` IS YMD 1995 12 31
        `capacity` IS cap
        `works under a contract of service` IS elem "contract" flags
        `works under a platform work agreement` IS elem "pwa" flags
        `class` IS cls
        `a Government employee` IS elem "govt" flags
        `in a class the President has declared` IS elem "declared" flags
        `the contract was illegal at the time of the accident` IS elem "illegal" flags
        `ordinarily resident in Singapore` IS elem "resident" flags
        `employed by an employer in Singapore` IS elem "sg employer" flags
        `required by the employment to work outside Singapore` IS elem "required abroad" flags
        `employed as crew of a Singapore ship` IS elem "crew" flags

`no class` MEANS `none of the Third Schedule classes`
`emp` MEANS `as an employee`
`pw` MEANS `as a platform worker`
`plain employee` MEANS `worker` `emp` `no class` (LIST "contract", "resident", "sg employer")
`plain platform worker` MEANS `worker` `pw` `no class` (LIST "pwa", "resident")

GIVEN who IS A STRING, st IS A `Work stage`, earned IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Platform engagement`
`with` who `at` st `earning` earned MEANS
    `Platform engagement` WITH `operator` IS who, `stage` IS st, `earnings in the lookback period` IS earned

-- An accident: its date, the TRUE flags by name, and the platform engagements.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      flags IS A LIST OF STRING
      engs IS A LIST OF `Platform engagement`
GIVETH AN Accident
`accident on` d `having` flags `serving` engs MEANS
    Accident WITH
        `date` IS d
        `in Singapore` IS NOT elem "abroad" flags
        `on a Singapore ship` IS elem "sg ship" flags
        `in the course of the work` IS elem "course" flags
        `evidence it did not arise out of the work` IS elem "contrary evidence" flags
        `travelling as a passenger to or from the workplace with the employer's permission` IS elem "passenger" flags
        `transport operated by or for the employer, or by arrangement with the employer` IS elem "employer transport" flags
        `transport operated in the ordinary course of a public transport service` IS elem "public transport" flags
        `in or about the workplace, or at work providing the platform service` IS elem "at workplace" flags
        `taking steps in an actual or supposed emergency to rescue, protect or avert damage` IS elem "emergency" flags
        `acting in contravention of law, regulations or orders, or without instructions` IS elem "contravening" flags
        `would otherwise have arisen out of and in the course of the work` IS elem "otherwise in course" flags
        `the act was done for the purposes of and in connection with the business or service` IS elem "for the business" flags
        `proven the injury is directly attributable to alcohol or a drug` IS elem "alcohol" flags
        `deliberate self-injury or deliberate aggravation` IS elem "self-injury" flags
        `injured in a fight or an assault` IS elem "fight" flags
        `assaulted another person in the fight` IS elem "assaulted" flags
        `any assault was in the exercise of the right of private defence` IS elem "private defence" flags
        `breaking up or preventing the fight, or safeguarding life, property or law and order` IS elem "breaking up" flags
        `under the instruction or with the consent of the employer or platform operator` IS elem "consent" flags
        `proven contravention of a Sixth Schedule Part 1 law in using a vehicle` IS elem "part 1" flags
        `used a vehicle in providing the platform service` IS elem "vehicle" flags
        `proven contravention of a Sixth Schedule Part 2 law about that vehicle` IS elem "part 2" flags
        `proven that contravention caused or contributed to the accident` IS elem "caused" flags
        `platform engagements` IS engs

`d0` MEANS YMD 2025 6 1
GIVEN flags IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH AN Accident
`emp accident` flags MEANS `accident on` `d0` `having` flags `serving` EMPTY

`stage 2 with A` MEANS LIST (`with` "A" `at` `work stage 2` `earning` 1000)

GIVEN flags IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH AN Accident
`pw accident` flags MEANS `accident on` `d0` `having` flags `serving` `stage 2 with A`

GIVEN f IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `employee liable with` f IF
    `is liable:` (`the liability for` `plain employee` `in the accident` (`emp accident` f))

GIVEN f IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `platform worker liable with` f IF
    `is liable:` (`the liability for` `plain platform worker` `in the accident` (`pw accident` f))

§§ `A. Coverage`

`at work` MEANS `emp accident` (LIST "course")
`at work abroad` MEANS `emp accident` (LIST "course", "abroad")

-- [A1] s 3(1)
#ASSERT `is covered:` (`the coverage of` `plain employee` `for the accident` `at work`)
-- [A2] Third Sch para 1
#ASSERT NOT `is covered:` (`the coverage of` (`worker` `emp` `a member of the Singapore Armed Forces` (LIST "contract", "resident")) `for the accident` `at work`)
-- [A3]/[A4] Third Sch para 2
#ASSERT NOT `is covered:` (`the coverage of` (`worker` `emp` `an officer of the Police Force, Civil Defence Force, Central Narcotics Bureau or Prisons Service` (LIST "contract", "resident")) `for the accident` `at work`)
-- [A5] Third Sch para 3
#ASSERT NOT `is covered:` (`the coverage of` (`worker` `emp` `a domestic worker employed in the domestic services of private premises` (LIST "contract", "resident")) `for the accident` `at work`)
-- [A6] s 3(1)(a) declared Government class
#ASSERT `is covered:` (`the coverage of` (`worker` `emp` `no class` (LIST "contract", "govt", "declared", "resident")) `for the accident` `at work`)
-- [A7] Government, not declared
#ASSERT NOT `is covered:` (`the coverage of` (`worker` `emp` `no class` (LIST "contract", "govt", "resident")) `for the accident` `at work`)
-- [A8] no contract of service
#ASSERT NOT `is covered:` (`the coverage of` (`worker` `emp` `no class` (LIST "resident")) `for the accident` `at work`)
-- [A9] s 9
#ASSERT `is covered:` (`the coverage of` (`worker` `emp` `no class` (LIST "contract", "resident", "sg employer", "required abroad")) `for the accident` `at work abroad`)
-- [A10] s 9(a) not resident
#ASSERT NOT `is covered:` (`the coverage of` (`worker` `emp` `no class` (LIST "contract", "sg employer", "required abroad")) `for the accident` `at work abroad`)
-- [A11] s 9(b) employer not in Singapore
#ASSERT NOT `is covered:` (`the coverage of` (`worker` `emp` `no class` (LIST "contract", "resident", "required abroad")) `for the accident` `at work abroad`)
-- [A12] s 65(2) seafarer on a Singapore ship abroad
#ASSERT `is covered:` (`the coverage of` (`worker` `emp` `no class` (LIST "contract", "crew")) `for the accident` (`emp accident` (LIST "course", "abroad", "sg ship")))
-- [A13] platform worker, 2025-02-01
#ASSERT `is covered:` (`the coverage of` `plain platform worker` `for the accident` (`accident on` (YMD 2025 2 1) `having` (LIST "course") `serving` `stage 2 with A`))
-- [A14] [A15] [A16] vintages
#ASSERT REFUSED `the coverage of` `plain employee` `for the accident` (`accident on` (YMD 2020 8 31) `having` (LIST "course") `serving` EMPTY)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the coverage of` `plain employee` `for the accident` (`accident on` (YMD 2020 9 1) `having` (LIST "course") `serving` EMPTY)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the coverage of` `plain employee` `for the accident` (`accident on` (YMD 2024 12 31) `having` (LIST "course") `serving` EMPTY)
-- [A17]
#ASSERT `is covered:` (`the coverage of` `plain employee` `for the accident` (`accident on` (YMD 2025 1 1) `having` (LIST "course") `serving` EMPTY))
-- [A18] platform worker 2024-12-31
#ASSERT REFUSED `the coverage of` `plain platform worker` `for the accident` (`accident on` (YMD 2024 12 31) `having` (LIST "course") `serving` `stage 2 with A`)
-- [A14] the liability answer refuses too
#ASSERT REFUSED `the liability for` `plain employee` `in the accident` (`accident on` (YMD 2020 8 31) `having` (LIST "course") `serving` EMPTY)

§§ `B. Accident liability — employees (s 7, s 8)`

-- [B1] s 7(1)
#ASSERT `employee liable with` (LIST "course")
-- [B2]/[B4] s 7(2)(a)
#ASSERT NOT `employee liable with` (LIST "course", "alcohol")
-- [B3] influence not proven directly attributable: the flag is false
#ASSERT `employee liable with` (LIST "course")
-- [B5]/[B6] s 7(2)(b)
#ASSERT NOT `employee liable with` (LIST "course", "self-injury")
-- [B7] fight, did not assault
#ASSERT `employee liable with` (LIST "course", "fight")
-- [B8] private defence
#ASSERT `employee liable with` (LIST "course", "fight", "assaulted", "private defence")
-- [B9] assaulted, no exception
#ASSERT NOT `employee liable with` (LIST "course", "fight", "assaulted")
-- [B10]/[B12] breaking up / safeguarding with employer's consent
#ASSERT `employee liable with` (LIST "course", "fight", "assaulted", "breaking up", "consent")
-- [B11] without consent
#ASSERT NOT `employee liable with` (LIST "course", "fight", "assaulted", "breaking up")
-- [B13] s 7(4) deemed
#ASSERT `employee liable with` (LIST "course")
-- [B14] evidence to the contrary
#ASSERT NOT `employee liable with` (LIST "course", "contrary evidence")
-- [B15] s 8(1)
#ASSERT `employee liable with` (LIST "passenger", "employer transport")
-- [B16] public transport
#ASSERT NOT `employee liable with` (LIST "passenger", "employer transport", "public transport")
-- [B17] no permission
#ASSERT NOT `employee liable with` (LIST "employer transport")
-- [B18] s 8(2)
#ASSERT `employee liable with` (LIST "at workplace", "emergency")
-- [B19] not at the workplace
#ASSERT NOT `employee liable with` (LIST "emergency")
-- [B20] s 8(3)
#ASSERT `employee liable with` (LIST "contravening", "otherwise in course", "for the business")
-- [B21] not for the business
#ASSERT NOT `employee liable with` (LIST "contravening", "otherwise in course")
-- s 8 deeming does not oust s 7(2): drunk on the company bus
#ASSERT NOT `employee liable with` (LIST "passenger", "employer transport", "alcohol")

§§ `C. Platform workers (ss 34D-34F)`

-- [C1]
#ASSERT `platform worker liable with` (LIST "course")
-- [C2] s 34D(2)(a)(i)
#ASSERT NOT `platform worker liable with` (LIST "course", "alcohol")
-- [C3] s 34D(2)(a)(ii): no causation needed
#ASSERT NOT `platform worker liable with` (LIST "course", "vehicle", "part 1")
-- [C4] Part 2 contravention that did not cause the accident
#ASSERT `platform worker liable with` (LIST "course", "vehicle", "part 2")
-- [C5] Part 2 contravention that caused it
#ASSERT NOT `platform worker liable with` (LIST "course", "vehicle", "part 2", "caused")
-- [C6]
#ASSERT NOT `platform worker liable with` (LIST "course", "self-injury")
-- [C7] breaking up a fight with the operator's consent
#ASSERT `platform worker liable with` (LIST "course", "fight", "assaulted", "breaking up", "consent")
-- [C8]
#ASSERT NOT `platform worker liable with` (LIST "course", "fight", "assaulted")
-- [C9] s 34F(1)
#ASSERT `platform worker liable with` (LIST "at workplace", "emergency")
-- [C10] s 34F(2)
#ASSERT `platform worker liable with` (LIST "contravening", "otherwise in course", "for the business")
-- employer transport (s 8(1)) is not applied to platform workers (s 34B replaces s 8 with s 34F)
#ASSERT NOT `platform worker liable with` (LIST "passenger", "employer transport")
-- [C13]/[C17] not at a work stage
#ASSERT NOT `is liable:` (`the liability for` `plain platform worker` `in the accident` (`accident on` `d0` `having` (LIST "course") `serving` (LIST (`with` "A" `at` `not at a work stage` `earning` 1000))))
-- [C18] A at stage 2, B at stage 1
`A2 B1` MEANS `accident on` `d0` `having` (LIST "course") `serving` (LIST (`with` "A" `at` `work stage 2` `earning` 1000), (`with` "B" `at` `work stage 1` `earning` 3000))
#ASSERT `share of` "A" `in` (`the liable platform operators and their shares for` `A2 B1`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `share of` "B" `in` (`the liable platform operators and their shares for` `A2 B1`) EQUALS 0
-- [C19] both at stage 1, earnings 3000 / 1000
`A1 B1` MEANS `accident on` `d0` `having` (LIST "course") `serving` (LIST (`with` "A" `at` `work stage 1` `earning` 3000), (`with` "B" `at` `work stage 1` `earning` 1000))
#ASSERT `share of` "A" `in` (`the liable platform operators and their shares for` `A1 B1`) EQUALS 0.75
#ASSERT `share of` "B" `in` (`the liable platform operators and their shares for` `A1 B1`) EQUALS 0.25
-- [C20] both at stage 2, equal earnings
`A2 B2` MEANS `accident on` `d0` `having` (LIST "course") `serving` (LIST (`with` "A" `at` `work stage 2` `earning` 2000), (`with` "B" `at` `work stage 2` `earning` 2000))
#ASSERT `share of` "A" `in` (`the liable platform operators and their shares for` `A2 B2`) EQUALS 0.5
-- a third operator not at a work stage takes no share
`A2 B2 Cn` MEANS `accident on` `d0` `having` (LIST "course") `serving` (LIST (`with` "A" `at` `work stage 2` `earning` 2000), (`with` "B" `at` `work stage 2` `earning` 2000), (`with` "C" `at` `not at a work stage` `earning` 9000))
#ASSERT `share of` "C" `in` (`the liable platform operators and their shares for` `A2 B2 Cn`) EQUALS 0

§§ `D. Principal (s 13)`

GIVEN biz IS A BOOLEAN, work IS A BOOLEAN, empd IS A BOOLEAN, place IS A BOOLEAN, dir IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Principal arrangement`
`principal` biz work empd place dir MEANS
    `Principal arrangement` WITH
        `contracted in the course of or for the principal's trade or business` IS biz
        `for execution of work, or supply of labour, undertaken by the principal` IS work
        `the employee was employed in executing the work` IS empd
        `accident at a place where the principal undertook to execute work, or under the principal's control` IS place
        `the Commissioner has directed the principal` IS dir

-- [D1]
#ASSERT `the principal is liable under s 13, the worker being` `emp` `:` (`principal` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- [D2] s 13(5)
#ASSERT NOT `the principal is liable under s 13, the worker being` `emp` `:` (`principal` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- no direction yet
#ASSERT NOT `the principal is liable under s 13, the worker being` `emp` `:` (`principal` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- [D5] s 34B(c)
#ASSERT NOT `the principal is liable under s 13, the worker being` `pw` `:` (`principal` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)

§§ `E. Disease (ss 10-12, 11A, 34G)`

GIVEN item IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      worked IS A BOOLEAN
      ceased IS A MAYBE DATE
      contracted IS A DATE
      chem IS A BOOLEAN
      exposureEnded IS A MAYBE DATE
      since2012 IS A BOOLEAN
      incap IS A MAYBE DATE
      died IS A MAYBE DATE
      cert IS A MAYBE DATE
      lastDay IS A DATE
      preceded IS A BOOLEAN
      specific IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Disease facts`
`disease` item worked ceased contracted chem exposureEnded since2012 incap died cert lastDay preceded specific MEANS
    `Disease facts` WITH
        `Second Schedule item` IS item
        `worked in the specified occupation when it was contracted` IS worked
        `ceased working in the specified occupation on` IS ceased
        `contracted on` IS contracted
        `directly attributable to a chemical or biological exposure at work` IS chem
        `exposure ceased on` IS exposureEnded
        `employed in that occupation by this employer on or after 1 June 2012` IS since2012
        `incapacity commenced on` IS incap
        `died on` IS died
        `certified as suffering from the disease on` IS cert
        `last day working for this employer or operator` IS lastDay
        `death preceded by compensable incapacity` IS preceded
        `directly attributable to a specific work injury` IS specific

