GIVEN wd IS A BOOLEAN, refusal IS A BOOLEAN, err IS A BOOLEAN, applied IS A BOOLEAN, heard IS A BOOLEAN, efma IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Refund facts`
`refund` wd refusal err applied heard efma MEANS
    `Refund facts` WITH
        `the claim was withdrawn and not resumed` IS wd
        `an order of refusal has been made or taken effect` IS refusal
        `paid on the basis of an error or false or misleading information` IS err
        `the payer applied in time, in the required form` IS applied
        `the claimant had a reasonable opportunity to make representations` IS heard
        `a medical payment the employer owes under the Employment of Foreign Manpower Act 1990` IS efma

